         <title><![CDATA[Chief William Commanda Bridge to remain open this winter]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/ottawa/chief-william-commanda-bridge-ottawa-gatineau-9.7437578?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/1.5896244,1795721649594/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1919%2C1079%29%3B' alt='A former rail bridge over a river in winter.' width='620' height='349' title='The Prince of Wales Bridge over the Ottawa River in January 2021. There are plans to turn the closed former rail bridge into a pedestrian and cyclist crossing by early 2022 and Mayor Jim Watson has added his voice to those wanting to rename it after Algonquin leader William Commanda when it opens.'/><p>For the first time in its short history, the Chief William Commanda pedestrian bridge between Ottawa and Gatineau, Que., will stay open over the winter.  It will not be maintained and users will do so at their own risk, according to the City of Ottawa.</p>]]></description>
